<h2> A note from the band </h2>
<b>Mazer Rackham</b> is a Boston based rock and roll band led by singer/songwriter Michael Moore.  Frequently compared to the Talking Heads, Elvis Costello and the Grateful Dead, they would prefer their first recording, Lies Heavy, be filed as psychedelic bluegrass punk.<p>

These recordings feature Michael Moore's guitar and vocals, Deborah Moore on bass, Josh Goldberg playing saxophones, Sarah Glynn on auxiliary guitar and violin 
and Sean Taylor playing the hybrid banjo/guitar monstrosity dubbed "The Wankee".<p>

Mazer lives and works in and around Boston, Massachusetts. <p>

